			</section>
			<section name="LabelGraphics">
				<attribute key="text" type="String">loanAmount = 1000;
interest = "20";

What will be the values of loanAmount+interest, loanAmount+loanAmount?</attribute>
				<attribute key="fontSize" type="int">12</attribute>
				<attribute key="fontName" type="String">Dialog</attribute>
				<attribute key="configuration" type="String">CroppingLabel</attribute>
				<attribute key="contentWidth" type="double">259.6621994461405</attribute>
				<attribute key="contentHeight" type="double">81.46875</attribute>
				<attribute key="autoSizePolicy" type="String">node_width</attribute>
				<attribute key="anchor" type="String">r</attribute>
			</section>
		</section>
		<section name="node">
			<attribute key="id" type="int">18</attribute>
			<attribute key="label" type="String">This is correct answer.

loanAmount is of int type, so loanAmount+loanAmount will do arithmetic addition. Thus, 1000+1000 will give 2000.

But interest is of string type, so loanAmount+interest will do string addition. Thus 1000+"20" will give "100020".

Note the use of double quotes for "20" and no double quotes for 1000.</attribute>
